---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, STUDIO } from '../../site';

const effective = 'September 25, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Shelly Jigsaw privacy policy"
  description="How the Shelly Jigsaw app by Ohana Studios handles your information, including ads from Google AdMob."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="card prose-card">
      <header class="page-head">
        <h1>Shelly Jigsaw privacy policy</h1>
        <p>Effective {effective}</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This policy explains what information the <strong>Shelly Jigsaw</strong> app for Android
          (package <code>com.ohanastudios.shellyjigsaw</code>) uses, why, and the choices you have.
          The app is made by {STUDIO} ("we", "us").
        </p>

        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You do not create an account, and we never ask for your name, email or photos.</li>
          <li>Your puzzle progress and settings stay on your phone. We do not receive them.</li>
          <li>We do not use analytics or tracking tools of our own.</li>
          <li>
            The game is free and shows ads from <strong>Google AdMob</strong>. Google collects some
            device information to show and measure those ads, as described below.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Information stored only on your phone</h2>
        <p>
          The app saves your puzzle progress, finished puzzles, stars and shells, Shelly's
          field notes, settings (such as text size, sound and vibration), and simple counters that decide how
          often ads appear. This information stays in the app's private storage on your device. It
          is not sent to us or to anyone else. Uninstalling the app, or clearing its data in
          Android settings, deletes it.
        </p>

        <h2>Ads from Google AdMob</h2>
        <p>
          Shelly Jigsaw shows three kinds of ads: a small banner below the puzzle while you play,
          an optional video you can choose to watch for an extra hint, and occasional full-screen
          ads between puzzles. Full-screen ads never interrupt a puzzle you are solving.
        </p>
        <p>
          The ads are provided by Google AdMob. When the app requests or shows an ad, Google may
          collect and process:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>device identifiers, such as your device's advertising ID and app set ID;</li>
          <li>your IP address, which can indicate your approximate location;</li>
          <li>information about your device, such as model, operating system and language;</li>
          <li>how you interact with ads, such as views and taps;</li>
          <li>diagnostic information, such as ad loading errors.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Google uses this information to deliver ads, limit how often you see the same ad,
          measure ad performance, prevent fraud and, where you allow it, show more relevant ads.
          This information is sent to Google, not to us. We only see anonymous, combined reports
          (for example, how many ads were shown). Google's use of this information is described in
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>
          and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices about ads</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland.</strong> If you are in these regions, the
            app asks for your consent through Google's consent message before personalized ads are
            shown. You can change your choice at any time with <strong>Privacy choices</strong> in
            the game's Settings.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Advertising ID.</strong> You can reset or delete your advertising ID, or opt out
            of personalized ads, in your phone's settings (usually
            <em>Settings &gt; Google &gt; Ads</em> or <em>Settings &gt; Privacy &gt; Ads</em>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Personalized ads in general.</strong> You can manage Google ad personalization at
            <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com" rel="noopener">My Ad Center</a>.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you opt out of personalized ads, you will still see ads, but they will be less tailored.</p>

        <h2>Phone permissions</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Permission</th><th>Why the app uses it</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Internet and network state</td><td>To load ads. Puzzles are built into the app and do not need a connection.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Advertising ID</td><td>Used by Google AdMob as described above.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Vibration</td><td>For the gentle buzz when pieces fit. You can turn it off in Settings.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>The app does not access your photos, contacts, camera, microphone or precise location.</p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Shelly Jigsaw is made for adults and is not directed at children under 13. We do not
          knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided
          personal information, please contact us and we will help.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR in Europe or state laws in the
          United States), you may have the right to access, correct or delete personal information,
          or to opt out of its "sale" or "sharing" for targeted advertising. Because we do not hold
          personal information about you, most requests are best handled by the choices above or
          directly with Google. We are happy to help with any request: just email us.
        </p>

        <h2>Security and retention</h2>
        <p>
          Your game data never leaves your device, so we do not store it. Information collected by
          Google for ads is kept according to Google's own retention policies.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change how the app uses information, we will update this page and its effective
          date. Important changes will also be mentioned in the app's store listing.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          {STUDIO}<br />
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
